.TH "SPEK" "1" "2023-01-09" "User\[cq]s Guide" "Version 0.8.5"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
Spek - Acoustic Spectrum Analyser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[C]spek\f[R] [\f[I]OPTION\f[R] \f[I]\&...\f[R]] [\f[I]FILE\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[I]Spek\f[R] generates a spectrogram for the input audio file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-h\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--help\f[B]\f[R]
Output the help message then quit.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-V\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--version\f[B]\f[R]
Output version information then quit.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-c\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--cli\f[B]\f[R]
Run without the graphical interface, see \f[B]BATCH PROCESSING\f[R] below.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-i\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--input\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]PATH\f[R]
Audio file or directory to analyse.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-o\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--output\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]PATH\f[R]
PNG file to write, or a directory when analysing more than one file.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-w\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--width\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Width of the image in pixels, 1024 by default.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-H\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--height\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Height of the image in pixels, one pixel per FFT band by default.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--fft-bits\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Size of the DFT window: 2^N samples, 11 (2048 samples) by default.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--stream\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Audio stream to analyse, zero-based.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--channel\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Audio channel to analyse, zero-based.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--min-db\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Lower limit of the dynamic range in dBFS, -120 by default.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--max-db\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Upper limit of the dynamic range in dBFS, 0 by default.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--palette\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]NAME\f[R]
Palette to use: sox (the default), spectrum or mono.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]--window\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]NAME\f[R]
DFT window function: hann (the default), hamming or blackman-harris.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-r\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--recursive\f[B]\f[R]
Recurse into the sub-directories of the input directory.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-j\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--jobs\f[B]\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
Number of files to analyse in parallel.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]-q\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]--quiet\f[B]\f[R]
Do not print the progress information.
.SH BATCH PROCESSING
.PP
Without \f[C]--cli\f[R] \f[I]Spek\f[R] opens the graphical interface.
When \f[C]--cli\f[R] (or \f[C]--input\f[R]) is given, \f[I]Spek\f[R]
analyses the files and saves the spectrograms as PNG images without opening a
window:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
spek --cli --input song.flac --output song.png
spek --cli --input ~/Music --output spectrograms --recursive --jobs 4
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
When the input is a directory, every file with a known audio extension is
analysed and the images are written into the output directory (or next to the
input files when \f[C]--output\f[R] is omitted), keeping the name of the
source file.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Notes
.PP
On OS X use the Command key instead of Ctrl.
.SS Menu
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]Ctrl-O\f[B]\f[R]
Open a new file.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]Ctrl-S\f[B]\f[R]
Save the spectrogram as an image file.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]Ctrl-E\f[B]\f[R]
Show the preferences dialog.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]F1\f[B]\f[R]
Open online manual in the browser.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]Shift-F1\f[B]\f[R]
Show the about dialog.
.SS Spectrogram
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]c\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]C\f[B]\f[R]
Change the audio channel.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]f\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]F\f[B]\f[R]
Change the DFT window function.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]l\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]L\f[B]\f[R]
Change the lower limit of the dynamic range in dBFS.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]p\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]P\f[B]\f[R]
Change the palette.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]s\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]S\f[B]\f[R]
Change the audio stream.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]u\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]U\f[B]\f[R]
Change the upper limit of the dynamic range in dBFS.
.TP
\f[B]\f[CB]w\f[B]\f[R], \f[B]\f[CB]W\f[B]\f[R]
Change the DFT window size.
.SH FILES
.TP
